  "contract": [
    "Allocate836 bytes, return null on allocation failure, assemble two352-byte graph records at offsets4/356, then dense/recurrent/executor records through byte835. No invented graph failure guard or cleanup.",
    "Dense24-byte descriptor preserves float representation bits, truncates flags to bytes and advances cursor with wrapping32-bit dimension arithmetic. Cursor aliases into output preserve copy-after-update behavior.",
    "Recurrent descriptor allocates units*4 bytes and clears before checking null. Live cursor is loaded after allocation; both three-byte matrix spans round up to4 and the tail advances by4*(units*10+6).",
    "The complete instance, descriptor records, cursor endpoints, unchanged address bindings and state zeroing have independent mathematical oracles in addition to paired stock/C execution."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Five entries total478 native bytes;476 executed. The two-byte branch at0x9910a is unreachable after the explicit return. No executable stock is retained in C.",
    "The graph builder at0x4387c and four opaque executor address data bindings remain unresolved. Address words establish identity only; no executor callable ABI or inference behavior is claimed.",
    "5794 paired cases use actual compiled C memory primitives; graph/allocation ports modeled.128 full C constructor/heap/teardown cases model only graph and executor bindings;836-byte instance and64-byte recurrent state are allocated and released by real C code.",
    "Resource pointers are normalized only for complete heap comparison, never rewritten during execution. Overflow cases prove logical word layouts, not physically valid enormous allocations.",
    "Cold floating-point activation, concurrency, malformed pointers, physical fault width, numerical inference and device behavior remain unproven. Broad memory write hooks are disabled following the independently established Unicorn discrepancy.",
    "884-unit ld -r composition passes without failures or duplicate strong symbols. Application imports increase63 to67 as one high-level import is replaced by five lower-level dependencies; boot remains22.873 existing nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged. No new writable state.",
    "This is relocatable composition, not a final executable, startup integration or bootable firmware proof."
